{"severity":"error","file":"errors/role_needs_invalid_1.march","start_line":13,"start_col":4,"end_line":13,"end_col":5,"message":"Protocol `Logging`: `C` may crash, so `C -> I : ...` needs `or crash do ... end`: what does `I` do if `C` crashes before sending?","code":"role_needs_invalid","fix":{"kind":"insert","after_line":13,"text":"      or crash do\n        I -> L : String\n      end"},"labels":[],"notes":["The crash branch is the rest of the conversation when `C` is gone. It must begin, for `L`, with a message from `I`; the fix sends one each, for you to change to what the conversation should do."],"category":"PROTOCOL"}
